From 97150fcca804b314731ea15458ad3462a438eb5a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: cruz <cruz@tbu.net>
Date: Wed, 19 Aug 2026 18:48:32 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 015/206] feat(shorebird): match their flag help text;
 print_dispatch_table_debug_info_to

Two findings, both from xref-ing their arm64 slice rather than from running it.

1. print_dispatch_table_debug_info_to is a DEAD FLAG in their own binary.
   It was recorded as "silent on a base build", implying some trigger we had
   not found. There is none: the global FLAG_print_dispatch_table_debug_info_to
   (0x100526798) has zero code references in their gen_snapshot. Verified two
   independent ways -- a register-tracking xref, and a high-recall scan of all
   720 adrp sites hitting page 0x100526000 for a nearby 0x798 immediate, whose
   only hits are `str x8, [x19, #0x798]` in Thread::InitVMConstants, an
   unrelated Thread field. It is registered so --help prints it, and never
   read. So it is declared here and left unread, which reproduces it exactly.
   The "11 private flags" are really 10 implementable plus this one.

2. Our six link-info flag descriptions were paraphrases, so --help did not
   match theirs. Replaced with their verbatim text. All 8 flags we claim now
   produce byte-identical --help --verbose lines.

Flag surface after this commit -- they have 263 flags, we have 300:
  they have / we lack:  3  (print_dd_function_identity_to,
                            print_dd_resolution_to, print_shorebird_info)
  we have / they lack: 40  (profiler, coverage, verify_after_gc, trace_*,
                            reload_*, deoptimize_*, use_osr, interpreter, ...)

The 3 missing are exactly the DD/linker ones already known to be blocked. All
40 extras are stock flags gated behind !PRODUCT, which says their build is
--mode=product where ours is --mode=release. Followed up separately, since a
PRODUCT build changes VM data structure layout and therefore bears on the
snapshot version hash difference.

Co-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>

diff --git a/runtime/vm/shorebird/link_info.cc b/runtime/vm/shorebird/link_info.cc
index eec03294032..2998b17275b 100644
--- a/runtime/vm/shorebird/link_info.cc
+++ b/runtime/vm/shorebird/link_info.cc
@@ -24,30 +24,43 @@
 
 namespace dart {
 
+// Descriptions are copied verbatim from their gen_snapshot's --help --verbose.
+// The CLI surface is part of what we are reproducing, so paraphrasing here
+// would be a diff against them for no benefit.
 DEFINE_FLAG(charp,
             print_class_table_link_info_to,
             nullptr,
-            "Write class table link info as a binary file");
+            "Print class table link information to the given file");
 DEFINE_FLAG(charp,
             print_class_table_link_debug_info_to,
             nullptr,
-            "Write class table link info as JSON, for debugging");
+            "Print class table link debug information to the given file");
 DEFINE_FLAG(charp,
             print_field_table_link_info_to,
             nullptr,
-            "Write field table link info as a binary file");
+            "Print field table link information to the given file");
 DEFINE_FLAG(charp,
             print_field_table_link_debug_info_to,
             nullptr,
-            "Write field table link info as JSON, for debugging");
+            "Print field table link debug information to the given file");
 DEFINE_FLAG(charp,
             print_dispatch_table_link_info_to,
             nullptr,
-            "Write dispatch table link info as a binary file");
+            "Print dispatch table link information to the given file");
 DEFINE_FLAG(charp,
             print_dispatch_table_link_debug_info_to,
             nullptr,
-            "Write dispatch table link info as JSON, for debugging");
+            "Print dispatch table link debug information to the given file");
+
+// Declared, never read -- and that is not an omission on our side. Their own
+// arm64 gen_snapshot never reads it either: the flag has zero code references
+// (verified two ways, see spikes/shorebird_linkinfo_oracle/scripts/xref.py),
+// which is why it stays silent on every build rather than only on a base build.
+// It exists so --help matches; there is no behaviour to reproduce.
+DEFINE_FLAG(charp,
+            print_dispatch_table_debug_info_to,
+            nullptr,
+            "Print layout of the dispatch table to a json file");
 
 namespace {
 
